# Go sources are scored against `gofmt`, which only accepts LF line endings. Without this the
# repository's own `core.autocrlf=true` checkout rewrites every fixture to CRLF, and the reference
# solution is then charged a formatting finding it did not earn - the admission reported
# `go.gofmt.scan value=1` against a reference that is correctly formatted in every other respect.
#
# `* text=auto` keeps git's normal end-of-line handling; the explicit `eol=lf` below overrides it
# for the two trees whose bytes are evidence rather than prose.
* text=auto

*.go    text eol=lf
*.mod   text eol=lf
*.sum   text eol=lf
# C fixtures and harness sources are sealed into task manifests and compiled under `-Wpedantic`:
# their bytes are evidence, so a `core.autocrlf` checkout must not decide their digests (D-20-04).
plugins/languages/c/**/*.c    text eol=lf
plugins/languages/c/**/*.h    text eol=lf
